Pages = {2002-2011},
Month = {APR},
Abstract = {Postoperative nursing plays a crucial role in healthcare by preventing
   complications such as infections and thrombosis through timely risk
   assessment and intervention. However, current nursing tools lack dynamic
   and personalized predictive capabilities, limiting their effectiveness.
   This article proposes the parallel nursing framework, which integrates
   large language models (LLMs) with the virtual-real synergy of parallel
   systems, leveraging the artificial systems, computational experiments,
   and parallel execution (ACP) approach. The framework utilizes LLM agents
   to enable proactive, precise, and personalized risk management within a
   closed-loop system. Building on this framework, we developed NursingGPT,
   a multiagent system with monitoring, prediction, simulation, decision,
   and communication agents that analyze patient data and predict risks. It
   provides real-time, tailored nursing interventions to address diverse
   needs. Its applications in infection risk management, complication
   prevention, personalized care, and cross-institutional knowledge sharing
   highlight its potential to enhance patient recovery, improve nursing
   quality, and reduce complications, offering a scalable, intelligent
   solution for postoperative nursing.},
